    {"year": 2019, "seat_label": "At-Large", "reason": "other", "attempted": "Moises M. Rodrigues vacated one of the four at-large seats on 2019-07-03 when the council elected him to finish Mayor Bill Carpenter's term. NARROWED: the seat was demonstrably FILLED, not left vacant - the October 15, 2019 council minutes open 'The meeting was called to order at 703:pm with ten members present. Councillor Monahan absent', i.e. eleven seated members, whereas an unfilled at-large vacancy would leave ten seated and at most nine present with Monahan out. So this is NOT reason:'vacant'. What remains unknown is the appointee's NAME: the roll call names only the absentee, and the minutes body names councillors by surname only in vote breakdowns. Searched news coverage of Carpenter's death and the succession (WGBH, Boston Globe, CBS Boston); none names an at-large replacement. Next step would be the September 9 or September 23, 2019 minutes (URLs known: brockton.gov/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/City_Council_Minutes_090919.pdf and .../City_Council_Minutes_092319.pdf), where the swearing-in of the replacement would appear, or the July/August 2019 minutes covering the appointment vote itself.", "notes": "Affects roughly half of 2019 for one of four at-large seats. The other three at-large seats for 2019 are sourced. Sole remaining gap in the file."}
